{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01011",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.69,
      "end_seconds": 3.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Good afternoon, you know, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.16,
      "end_seconds": 9.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 9.84,
      "end_seconds": 22.59,
      "duration_seconds": 12.75,
      "text": "honestly, it's bloating after milk or ice cream, and my family pushed me to come i'm hoping you can tell me something definite"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.05,
      "end_seconds": 26.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "is it worse at certain times?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.24,
      "end_seconds": 32.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "I notice it more with ice cream"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.74,
      "end_seconds": 37.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Okay, is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.17,
      "end_seconds": 42.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "it feels mild to to me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.97,
      "end_seconds": 46.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Is it accompanied by anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.32,
      "end_seconds": 57.16,
      "duration_seconds": 8.84,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get cramps as well. I've also had rumbling and gas."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.36,
      "end_seconds": 62.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "have you had any vomiting, rash or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.85,
      "end_seconds": 67.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "no, um, not a single one"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.28,
      "end_seconds": 74.4,
      "duration_seconds": 6.12,
      "text": "okay, go on have you had any night-time symptoms or blood in the stool?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.07,
      "end_seconds": 81.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "no night-time symptoms or blood in the stool, none of it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.06,
      "end_seconds": 85.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Any breathing difficulties apart from this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.09,
      "end_seconds": 88.06,
      "duration_seconds": 0.97,
      "text": "Breathing's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.37,
      "end_seconds": 91.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Any trouble with the waterworks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.4,
      "end_seconds": 93.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "No changes there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.71,
      "end_seconds": 99.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.39,
      "end_seconds": 117.31,
      "duration_seconds": 16.92,
      "text": "I'm on escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day a neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it i had aspirin at one point, but I'm off it now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.0,
      "end_seconds": 123.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "so, what conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.16,
      "end_seconds": 127.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Anxiety, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.59,
      "end_seconds": 134.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Is there anything more?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.23,
      "end_seconds": 137.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "I have heart disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.29,
      "end_seconds": 145.89,
      "duration_seconds": 7.6,
      "text": "right, right okay, I can see anxiety and heart disease in your file as well"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.44,
      "end_seconds": 164.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.53,
      "end_seconds": 169.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.31,
      "end_seconds": 172.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "and your job?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.53,
      "end_seconds": 177.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "I work in accounts at a hospital."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.35,
      "end_seconds": 180.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.55,
      "end_seconds": 188.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.91,
      "end_seconds": 192.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "So, how are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.27,
      "end_seconds": 198.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.95,
      "end_seconds": 221.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.15,
      "end_seconds": 229.38,
      "duration_seconds": 6.23,
      "text": "Not currently, but as a youngster trimethoprim gave me a rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.73,
      "end_seconds": 233.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "let me take your readings now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.22,
      "end_seconds": 245.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.25,
      "end_seconds": 278.16,
      "duration_seconds": 16.91,
      "text": "Okay: weight 95 kilos, pulse is 75 beats a minute, BMI works out to 38.1, height 158 centimetres, BP is 119 over 82, oxygen saturation is 99 percent, temp 36.7 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.18,
      "end_seconds": 282.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "is that alright, uh, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.01,
      "end_seconds": 286.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "We'll look at it together shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.4,
      "end_seconds": 291.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.13,
      "end_seconds": 296.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.97,
      "end_seconds": 319.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft and non-tender, with active bowel sounds."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.39,
      "end_seconds": 325.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.47,
      "end_seconds": 352.84,
      "duration_seconds": 9.37,
      "text": "Let me tell you where I've got to. I can't pin this down yet. We're looking at lactose intolerance or coeliac disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 353.49,
      "end_seconds": 356.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 358.8,
      "end_seconds": 371.61,
      "duration_seconds": 12.81,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with lactose intolerance do well once it's treated properly. I want a hydrogen breath test done, that's for suspected lactose intolerance."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 373.54,
      "end_seconds": 375.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "that's fine with me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 377.4,
      "end_seconds": 395.39,
      "duration_seconds": 17.99,
      "text": "I think a coeliac test makes sense here, for bloating. Try two weeks without dairy and tell me if it makes a difference. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 395.66,
      "end_seconds": 414.43,
      "duration_seconds": 18.77,
      "text": "Yes. If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. I'd like to to see you again in three weeks. Let me check I've been clear. What will you do once you get home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 416.27,
      "end_seconds": 421.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "so, I come back in three weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 422.54,
      "end_seconds": 429.67,
      "duration_seconds": 7.13,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. So, is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 431.6,
      "end_seconds": 434.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Thank you, uh, that's helpful."
    }
  ]
}